WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.503
MEMO: It's magical
just to be here.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:07.640
I'm thinking about how
many thousands of stones

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.176
are overhead, man.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.246
So let's not think
a lot about that.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.748
KENNY BROAD: My
name is Kenny Broad.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.249
I'm the mission specialist.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.218
NARRATOR: Kenny Broad
is a National Geographic

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.487
explorer and chief
exploration officer

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.988
of the Virtual Wonders Team.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.425
MAN: I would describe Kenny
Broad as a mad scientist.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.360
NARRATOR: As an expert
caver, he and Memo

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.230
may be able to add crucial
insight on how to access

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.464
the chamber below the pyramid.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.899
MEMO: There's very
few people that have

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.067
the privilege to go in here.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.168
KENNY BROAD: I
don't want to wait.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.836
MEMO: All right, let's go.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.705
KENNY BROAD: Being involved
in a new discovery,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.708
it gives you this feeling
that you're doing something

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:44.511
larger than just yourself.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.446
NARRATOR: While there are
no portals to the underworld

00:00:46.513 --> 00:00:50.083
on the ground floor, they hike
up to a sacred chamber, which

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.152
holds some intriguing clues.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:56.723
MEMO: And this is
the amazing room.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.628
So beware.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.462
KENNY BROAD: Wow.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.264
Oh, my gosh, that's incredible.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.669
MEMO: Yeah, this is where
the king used to sit.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:13.006
NARRATOR: This is
the jaguar throne.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:15.041
KENNY BROAD: So the
king used to sit here.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:18.311
I mean, it really sticks out
because it still has, I assume,

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:19.746
the original paint?

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.047
MEMO: Yes.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.549
NARRATOR: From
this royal throne,

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:26.085
kings watched countless
humans sacrificed to the rain

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.855
god Chaac at this nearby altar.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:37.297
Could their remains lie
in the veiled crypt below?

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.766
KENNY BROAD: Those are
the original insets?

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.934
Is that jade?

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.735
MEMO: This is jade.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.406
NARRATOR: To the Maya, jade
was a royal resource, used

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.475
to communicate with the gods.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.276
KENNY BROAD: But there's
no local jade, so--

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.611
MEMO: Exactly.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.813
Yeah, they bring it all
the way from Guatemala.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.382
It was one very important item.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:59.486
Only Royalty had access to it.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.288
This context is not
only a royal context,

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:07.727
where the king used to rest,
sit, it's also a funerary one.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.798
There is a relationship
with death here and life.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.700
KENNY BROAD: Resurrection?
MEMO: Resurrection.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.667
KENNY BROAD: The cycle.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.135
[inaudible] is the cycle.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.637
NARRATOR: The
ornate jaguar throne

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:21.274
sits in front of something
even more grim and ominous.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.346
MEMO: This is an amazing
wall for a number of reasons.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:30.650
And what we see here
is embedded bones.

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:36.856
They are long human bones
that are embedded on the wall.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:44.297
There's one there, another
one here, and there.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.366
My assumption as a
bioarchaeologist,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.568
I believe these are leg bones.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.403
KENNY BROAD: That looks
like it'd be a femur or--

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.605
MEMO: Exactly, or tibias.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:55.008
If you ask me, I would
say, yeah, that might

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.644
represent bones of ancestors--

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.778
KENNY BROAD: Right.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.346
MEMO: --or people very powerful.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.681
KENNY BROAD: What's
your sense of what

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.149
can be behind this wall?

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:07.353
MEMO: Well, I do really
believe that there is something

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.156
intentionally positive there.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:13.993
Given the sacredness of
the site, the importance

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.062
of the place within
Chichen Itza,

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.065
I believe it could be
a burial back there.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.833
KENNY BROAD: I mean,
it makes logical sense.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.402
MEMO: It makes sense, yes.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:27.006
Yet, if somebody is buried
here, it was for sure a very

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:30.243
important person, a king.

